        'howto.goal_title':          'Goal',
        'howto.goal_desc':           "Chop every tree on the map to expand your territory. The game ends once none are left.",
        'howto.villagers_title':     'Villagers',
        'howto.villagers_desc':      'Recruit villagers with wood, food or textiles and assign them to a building (farm, quarry, lumber camp...) so they work it on their own.',
        'howto.cityAdjacency_title': 'City buildings',
        'howto.cityAdjacency_desc':  "House, Bakery, Church, Workshop, Tax Office, Tavern, City Market, Theatre and Sawmill all need to sit right against ANOTHER city building (or the Town Center) AND have a connected road nearby. Otherwise they're isolated and don't count — an isolated house, for example, adds no population.",
        'howto.roads_title':         'Roads',
        'howto.roads_desc':          "Every other building (farms, quarries, lumber camps...) only needs to touch any connected road or the Town Center — it doesn't need to sit next to another building.",
        'howto.skills_title':        'Skill Tree',
        'howto.skills_desc':         'Find relics while exploring the map to unlock permanent upgrades in the skill tree.',
        'howto.legado_title':        'Legacy (Prestige)',
        'howto.legado_desc':         'Reaching certain relic milestones lets you reset the run in exchange for permanent bonuses that stick around forever, even after the reset.',
        'howto.tip_well_title':      'Water your farms',
        'howto.tip_well_desc':       'A Well next to a farm gives it ×3 harvest speed and ×2 carry capacity. It needs no road and it is cheap: build one whenever you can.',
        'howto.tip_mules_title':     'Keep the two markets apart',
        'howto.tip_mules_desc':      'Mules bring back more gold the further the Rural Market is from the City Market, and the bonus grows faster than the distance does. What counts is the gap between the two buildings, not how far the mule walks: a zig-zagging road only makes it slower.',
        'howto.tip_tavern_title':    'Taverns',
        'howto.tip_tavern_desc':     'With its Pension upgrade, a Tavern gives +1 population per house within 3 tiles. With two Taverns, a house inside both areas only counts once: spread them out so they cover different houses.',
        'howto.tip_forest_title':    'When the forest runs out',
        'howto.tip_forest_desc':     'Felled trees never grow back. The Timber Plantation is the only source of wood that never runs dry.',
        'wipe.btn.cancel':      'Cancel',
